          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 310,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:1",
          "start": 171
        },
        "quote": "(b) Minor Streets. In residential areas of subdivisions all streets shall be of a design which will discourage through or nonlocal traffic.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.40.050 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "ef0960fa-24d4-5bd4-a8de-1be6f7c54963",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 464,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:2",
          "start": 311
        },
        "quote": "(c) Culs-de-sac. Culs-de-sac in subdivisions shall normally be no longer than 500 feet, including a turnaround which shall be provided at the closed end.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.40.050 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "c36dd26f-c1cf-576c-b05a-63d4ffb05b37",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 747,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:3",
          "start": 465
        },
        "quote": "(d) Right Angle Intersections. Under normal conditions, streets in subdivisions shall be laid out to intersect, as nearly as possible, at right angles. Where topography or other conditions justify a variation from the right angle intersection, the minimum angle shall be 60 degrees.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.40.050 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "7df713ac-78f2-5326-ba7f-f95aed961f5c",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1346,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:4",
          "start": 748
        },
        "quote": "(e) Streets Adjacent to a Railroad Right-of-Way, Limited Access Freeway or Other Major Thoroughfares. A marginal access street or frontage road in a subdivision shall be provided parallel and adjacent to the boundary of rights-of-way of railroads, limited access freeways and major traffic thoroughfares; however, a street may be provided at a distance suitable for the appropriate use of land between such street and such rights-of-way. Such distance shall be determined with due consideration of the minimum distance required for approach connections to future grade separation or for lot depths.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.40.050 block 5",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 5,
          "component_id": "0505bd2f-11c9-5a2d-8002-84956e5ca3d3",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1561,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:5",
          "start": 1347
        },
        "quote": "(f) Half-Streets. Dedication of half-streets will not be approved except where such streets are essential to the reasonable development of the subdivision and in conformity with other requirements of this division.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:5#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.40.050 block 6",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 6,
          "component_id": "a1681c6f-0cb9-56f8-8a17-afddab480864",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2073,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:6",
          "start": 1562
        },
        "quote": "(g) Alleys. Alleys shall be provided in commercial and industrial districts, except that this requirement may be waived where other definite and assured provisions are made for service access, such as off-street loading, unloading and parking consistent with and adequate for the uses proposed. Dead-end alleys shall be avoided wherever possible, but if unavoidable, such dead-end alleys may be approved if adequate turnaround facilities are provided at the closed end. (Code 1981 § 41-93. Code 1995 § 134-135.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.050:block:6#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
